# Couple two cases: two plain OpenFOAM cases (a buoyantPimpleFoam channel and a laplacianFoam plate, no preCICE in them)
# made into a CHT coupled case: the form asks what the adapter needs (k for laplacianFoam), checks the time step against
# the window, copies both, writes precice-config.xml, the preciceDicts, the adapter and the interface conditions; the
# coupled run then goes with real OpenFOAM through preCICE. The original cases are left as they were.
click nav:coupling
wait-until page Coupling
click cpl-build
wait-until modal any timeout 5
choose cb-case#0 fluidCase   (cplpair)
wait 5
choose cb-patch#0 interface
choose cb-case#1 solidCase   (cplpair)
wait 5
choose cb-patch#1 interface
wait 5
assert text needs the conductivity k
assert not enabled cb-go
click cb-k#1
type 100
wait 5
assert text time windows of 0.01 s up to 0.1 s (10 windows)
assert text 2-D meshes
click cb-out
key A ctrl
type chtBuilt
screenshot $OUT/cpl_build.png
click cb-go
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
assert text Temperature
assert file precice-config.xml
assert log fluid-openfoam/system/preciceDict participant Fluid;
assert log solid-openfoam/system/preciceDict k   [ 1  1 -3 -1 0 0 0 ] 100;
assert not file $SB/ws/cplpair/fluidCase/system/preciceDict
click nav:run
wait 10
click cpl-go
wait-until toast Started 2 participants timeout 20
wait-until toast Coupled run finished timeout 400
assert log fluid-openfoam/log.Fluid End
assert log solid-openfoam/log.Solid End
assert log fluid-openfoam/precice-Fluid-iterations.log 10
screenshot $OUT/cpl_build_done.png
